  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone $(x-2)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2}=2{z}^{2}$ and the plane $x+2z-3=0$ onto the $yz$-plane?",
  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx+2z-3=0\\,⟹\\,x=3-2z\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2z-2)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} & =2{z}^{2} \\\\ (1-2z)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} & =2{z}^{2} \\\\ 1-4z+4{z}^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} & =2{z}^{2} \\\\ 2{z}^{2}-4z+1+2(y+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2(z-1)^{2}-2+1+2(y+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2(z-1)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (y+1)^{2}+(z-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a circle of radius $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane.",
